window.BP.decisionsMarkdown = "# Prototype decisions and demo defaults\n\nThe prototype needs an answer for some items the client has **not decided yet**. This file lists every such default and every assumption made while building, so each can be shown to the client and confirmed or changed.\n\n- **Demo default:** comes from CLAUDE.md Section 8. Not a client decision.\n- **Assumption:** made while planning or building the prototype. Not a client decision.\n- \"Plan Q#\" points to the open question number in `docs/BoodhamPSC_Application_Plan.md` Section 14.\n\nLast updated: 20 Oct 2026 (requested current affairs, test review and mock updates).\n\n## Answered by the team (8 Oct 2026)\n\n| Question | Answer | Effect on the prototype |\n|---|---|---|\n| Reference screens | None coming; design it ourselves | All screens are designed from the design system. The three images stay style references only. |\n| Logo | No logo yet; design a custom one | Custom ghost mark (\"Boodham\" means ghost) plus a \"BoodhamPSC\" wordmark. Placeholder until a real logo exists. |\n| Creator editing | Creators can edit at any time; nothing goes live until the admin approves | See B22 and B23. |\n| Sample papers | Sample papers written for the demo are fine | See B31. |\n\n---\n\n## A. Demo defaults (CLAUDE.md Section 8)\n\n| # | Item | Demo default | Plan Q# |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| A1 | Negative mark value | 1/3 of the question's marks when negative marking is on | Q5 |\n| A2 | Options per question | Always 4 | Q6 |\n| A3 | Special Topic and Sectional | Paper Test template (Admin can switch either card to Topic Test) | Q4 |\n| A4 | Mock cards and UPSC/PSC | Use Prelims/Mains, no Year | – |\n| A5 | PYQ 10th / 12th / Degree | Use Prelims/Mains and Year | – |\n| A6 | Retake limit | None | Q7 |\n| A7 | Current affairs practice | One question at a time, answer and correct option shown right after choosing, with Next | Q8 |\n| A8 | Current affairs access | Free | Q9 |\n| A9 | Current affairs past months | Removed from the prototype; only Daily, Weekly and Monthly are shown | Superseded by the 20 Oct 2026 request |\n| A10 | Current affairs periods | Daily: 0–6 days old · Weekly: 7–27 days old, grouped as Week N + month · Monthly: 28+ days old, grouped by publish month | Superseded by the 20 Oct 2026 request |\n| A11 | Notification alerts | Sent to all users | Q10 |\n| A12 | Notification official link | Optional field, shown as a button if filled | Q11 |\n| A13 | Plan | One monthly plan, sample price ₹199/month, marked \"sample price\" in Admin | Q2 |\n| A14 | Banner start/end dates | Not built | Q13 |\n| A15 | Admin creating tests | Not in the prototype. Admin only manages structure, banners and approvals | Q14 |\n\n---\n\n## B. Assumptions made for the prototype\n\n### Look and feel\n| # | Assumption | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| B1 | The three reference images (all from a product called \"Acadence\") are used for **style only**: colours, type, shapes, spacing, components. No layout or content is copied. Every BoodhamPSC screen is our own design. | None of them is a BoodhamPSC screen; confirmed no others are coming. |\n| B2 | Font: **Urbanist** for all English UI; **Noto Sans Malayalam** for Malayalam. | Closest Google Font to the references' geometric single-storey \"a\". |\n| B3 | Logo: a friendly ghost on a blue-to-violet rounded tile, plus the wordmark \"Boodham**PSC**\". Replace when a real logo exists. | \"Boodham\" (ഭൂതം) means ghost. Team asked for a custom logo. |\n| B4 | No dark mode, global search, charts or leaderboard, even though the references show them. | Not confirmed features. |\n| B5 | User app navigation: bottom bar (Home, Alerts, Profile) below 1024px wide; top bar with the same links on desktop. Creator and Admin use a left sidebar (drawer on mobile). | CLAUDE.md and master context; sidebar matches the references. |\n| B6 | Avatars are initials, not photos. | No real people in sample data. |\n\n### User app\n| # | Assumption | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| B7 | Logging in with the seeded demo phone number skips onboarding (returning user). Any other number is treated as a new user and goes through onboarding. The demo panel also has \"Log in as demo user\". | Lets story 1 (new user) and story 2 (user with history) both work. |\n| B8 | OTP accepts any 4 or 6 digits; a hint on screen says so. | Demo only. |\n| B9 | Year chips on Paper Test cards show only years that have at least one published test for that card and stage, newest first. If none, an empty state is shown. Paper Download years work the same per category. | Avoids rows of empty years. The shared Years list still drives what Creators can pick. |\n| B10 | Topic Test: if a subject has no subsections, the user goes straight from subject to its test list. | CLAUDE.md \"Subsection (if the subject has any)\". |\n| B11 | The 60-second window counts real time: the test timer keeps running while the user is away or reconnecting, as a server timer would. | Matches \"server-controlled timer\". |\n| B12 | Heartbeat every 5 seconds while the test screen is open. | Demo value; the real app decides its own interval. |\n| B13 | Answers are saved per selection; changing an answer overwrites it. A user can clear a selection by tapping the selected option again. | Common exam UX; nothing confirmed against it. |\n| B14 | \"Skip\" moves to the next question without answering. A question counts as **skipped** if it was seen but not answered; **not visited** if never opened. On the result, both count as skipped. | Result has only correct / wrong / skipped. |\n| B15 | Score is shown to two decimals (e.g. 6.67 / 10) and can be negative. | Negative marking at 1/3. |\n| B16 | Each attempt stores a snapshot of the test, so its result and review never change, even if the test is later edited or unpublished. | Master context: \"Result is written once\". |\n| B17 | Premium unlock is instant and the demo subscription does not expire in the prototype. Subscription expiry rules are not shown. | Expiry rule is still \"to confirm\" (Plan Q3). |\n| B18 | Payment sheet is a generic \"Payment (demo)\" with UPI / Card / Net banking choices and no third-party logos. Pay always succeeds. | CLAUDE.md rule 7. |\n| B19 | Paper \"download\" gives a small generated text/PDF-like sample file named after the paper, plus a toast. | No real files in the prototype. |\n| B20 | Current affairs practice progress is not scored or kept in history. | Not confirmed as a feature. |\n| B21 | Push-style alerts appear for notifications approved while the user was away, the next time the User app is viewed, one at a time. | CLAUDE.md 6.3. |\n\n### Creator and Admin\n| # | Assumption | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| B22 | Creators can edit their content **at any time, in any status**. Nothing they change reaches users until the admin approves it. Editing a **published** item creates \"pending changes\": users keep seeing the approved version until the admin approves the new one. Editing an item that is **in review** keeps it in review with the latest changes. | Team answer (8 Oct 2026). |\n| B23 | A **rejected** item (or rejected pending changes) keeps the admin's note visible while the Creator edits it, and returns to \"In review\" when resubmitted. If rejected pending changes belong to a published item, the published version stays live. | CLAUDE.md \"Edit and resubmit\" + B22. |\n| B24 | Creators can create content for Live and Coming soon cards, not Hidden ones. | Lets content be prepared before a card goes live. |\n| B25 | Notifications and current affairs have no free/premium step when approving. Papers and tests do. Tests also get negative marking on/off. | CLAUDE.md 6.5 and A8. |\n| B26 | Reordering sections and cards uses up/down buttons (works with keyboard and touch), not drag and drop. | Simpler and accessible for a prototype. |\n| B27 | Hiding a section hides all its cards from users. | Natural reading of \"hide section\". |\n| B28 | Deleting structure is not offered; Admin hides instead. | Avoids orphaned content in the demo. |\n| B29 | Banner images are a mock upload (shown from the local file for the session) or a colour/gradient preset. | No backend. |\n| B30 | Users and creators lists are view-only (search, subscription, attempts count). No ban/edit actions. | Only listing is confirmed. |\n\n### Structure details\n| # | Assumption | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| B35 | Special Topic and Sectional use Prelims/Mains **and** Year (they sit in the PYQ section). | A3 only fixes the template; their filters were not specified. |\n| B36 | The Coming soon cards SCERT and PDF are set to the Paper Download template, so they work the moment the admin sets them Live. | Every card needs a template. |\n| B37 | Topic subjects have an icon (picked by the admin) so the subject list is easy to scan. | Visual aid only. |\n| B38 | A section can be visible or hidden. A hidden section hides all its cards. | Same as B27. |\n| B39 | Papers, notifications and current affairs belong to the card they were created in. A second card using the same flow has its own content. | Keeps every card independent, as the configurable model needs. |\n| B40 | Banners can be deleted (structure items can only be hidden, see B28). | Banners are short-lived promotions. |\n\n### Tests and alerts (added while building)\n| # | Assumption | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| B41 | A user can have one test in progress at a time. Starting another shows a \"Resume it\" note on the rules page. | Keeps the timer and reconnect rules simple. |\n| B42 | **Retake** on the result page starts a fresh attempt straight away (via the rules page only if the test is now locked or another test is running). | CLAUDE.md: \"Retake starts a fresh attempt\". |\n| B43 | Alerts are sent the first time a notification is approved. Approving later edits to a live notification does not alert users again. | Avoids repeat alerts for small corrections. |\n| B44 | The rules page shows the user's previous attempts for that test, each opening its result. | Uses the confirmed attempt history; no new data. |\n| B45 | Login with a new number asks for the name first; the demo user (98765 43210) goes straight to Home. | B7. |\n\n### Sample data\n| # | Assumption | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| B31 | All PYQ and mock tests are **sample papers written for the demo**, not real Kerala PSC papers, and are labelled \"Sample\". | Confirmed by the team. Do not present invented papers as real. |\n| B32 | Tests reuse questions from one shared bilingual question bank of well-known facts (Kerala geography and history, Indian Constitution, general science, maths, English grammar). | Keeps every fact checkable. |\n| B33 | Sample notifications and current affairs are labelled \"Sample\" and contain no real dates or vacancies presented as real. Current affairs questions are general knowledge. | CLAUDE.md rule 7 and §10. |\n| B34 | **Malayalam translations must be checked by a native speaker** before the client demo goes wider. | Machine-assisted translation risk. |\n\n---\n\n### UI refinements (19 Oct 2026, requested by the team)\n| # | Decision | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| B46 | The test screen shows a permanent question-progress panel (Attempted / Skipped / Remaining, question grid, Submit) instead of a palette button and pop-up. Right side on desktop, a strip above the question on phones. | Team request: progress always visible. |\n| B47 | The question on screen counts as Remaining until the user leaves it unanswered; then it counts as Skipped. | Counts stay honest while the user is reading. |\n| B48 | Each section has a colour theme (violet, blue, teal, amber, rose) set by the admin; cards show a live count (\"5 tests\"). | Team request: colourful cards; theme is data, so new sections need no code. |\n| B49 | User app navigation: sidebar on desktop, icon rail on tablets, bottom tabs on phones. No avatar in the navigation; Profile is a menu item. | Team request. |\n| B50 | Premium has its own components (Go Premium button, member badge, sidebar card): night violet with a gold crown. | Team request: Premium should look and feel premium. |\n\n### Product UI updates (20 Oct 2026, requested by the client)\n| # | Decision | Effect on the prototype |\n|---|---|---|\n| B51 | Current affairs has Daily (days 0–6), Weekly (days 7–27) and Monthly (day 28 onward) only. Weekly content groups as “Week N [Month Year]”; monthly content groups by publication month. | Buckets are calculated from publish dates; there is no Past months tab. |\n| B52 | Current affairs subjects are entered by creators on each question and appear as a filter row in Monthly only. Admin can enable or disable the row per Current Affairs card. | Subject names are creator-entered text; the row is hidden when disabled or empty. |\n| B53 | Paper Test cards can optionally use a subject filter in addition to Prelims / Mains and Year. | Admin enables it per card and manages its subject choices in Structure; creators assign a subject to each test. |\n| B54 | Test attempts store elapsed time per question, and Review shows that time for each question. | Time accumulates while each question is active and is finalized when the user leaves it or submits. |\n| B55 | Review starts without revealing either answer. The user chooses an option to reveal their original answer, review answer, correct answer and explanation. | Review choices persist for the attempt and can be changed during the review. |\n| B56 | Creators provide English and Malayalam explanations for every question. | Both explanations are required before a question can be submitted; the review reveals the current-language explanation after a review choice. |\n| B57 | “Real PSC Mock” is a 100-question sample in Boodham PSC PYQ › 12th › Prelims › 2023, with a 90-minute duration and five subject groups: Current affairs, Maths, Reasoning, Malayalam and English (20 questions each). | Client confirmed the duration and five groups. This is a demo sample, not an official PSC paper; questions are bilingual sample content. |\n| B58 | On phones, test progress opens from a top-corner icon in a right-side drawer. Alerts remain available from the top-right bell and do not appear in the mobile bottom navigation. | Client requested a compact test view and top-right-only Alerts access on phones. |\n\n## C. Not built (pending with the client)\n\nStore, leaderboards, special-day quizzes, weak-area analysis, important-question bookmarks, question-paper sharing, bulk question upload, About page, shuffled options, admin reports (dashboard has simple tiles only), banner start/end dates, Admin-created content, subscription expiry flow, under-18 consent (Plan Q15), qualification-targeted alerts, Exam ↔ Application linking (Plan Q11), file format/size limits for papers (Plan Q12).\n\n---\n\n## D. Technical notes for the demo\n\n- **Demo login:** mobile number **98765 43210** (Anjali, has test history) or any other 10-digit number starting 6 to 9 to sign up as a new user. OTP: any 4 or 6 digits. Creator and Admin sign in by picking an account.\n- The demo panel has a **Component gallery** (prototype tool) that shows every shared component and colour. It is not part of the product.\n- Lightest text colour is `#6E737B` (slightly darker than the sampled `#7B8088`) so captions meet WCAG AA contrast.\n\n- Runs by double-clicking `index.html`. Fonts load from Google Fonts, so the Malayalam font needs an internet connection; without it the browser falls back to a system Malayalam font.\n- All data is in the browser's local storage. Demo › Reset demo data restores the seed.\n- Opening Admin in one tab and User in another works: changes appear in the other tab automatically.\n- Browser push is simulated with an in-app banner; real push needs the production app (and on iPhone, \"Add to Home Screen\").\n";
